lemma-calibrate
Copyright 2026 Epsilon Research

Extracted and generalized from the Epsilon internal quantitative research
codebase (per-project calibration scoring layer). The Murphy decomposition
follows Murphy (1973), "A New Vector Partition of the Probability Score";
Spiegelhalter's Z follows Spiegelhalter (1986), "Probabilistic prediction in
patient management and clinical trials"; the Wilson score interval follows
Wilson (1927). The in-package skills installer pattern is adapted from
goldmansachs/gs-quant (Apache-2.0). The optional ledger reader consumes the
event-log format of the superforecasting-skill ledger (deusyu/
superforecasting-skill, MIT) read-only; no code from that project is included.
